OPTION TO RENEW
This Option to Renew is attached to and becomes a part of that certain Shopping Center
Lease of even date herewith which has been or will be executed by and between Timothy B.
Sittema, Michael Bullock, El Del Range LLC, and Terra West LLC, collectively, jointly and
severally, as Landlord, and Vitamin Cottage Natural Food Markets, Inc., as Tenant.
The
consideration for this Option to Renew is the full and faithful performance of Tenant under the
Lease.
a.
Tenant is hereby granted the option to extend the Term of the Lease for five (5) five
(5)-year periods (each, an “Extension Term”) by giving notice of exercise of the option (“Option
Notice”) to Landlord as described in subparagraph c. below, before the expiration of the Initial
Lease Term, or the current Extension Term, as applicable, upon the same terms contained in this
Lease, excluding the provisions of this Exhibit I and except for the amount of Minimum Rent and
Additional Rent payable during each Extension Term; and any reference in the Lease to the “Term”
of the Lease shall be deemed to include any Extension Term and apply thereto, unless it is expressly
provided otherwise. Tenant shall have no additional extension options except as stated herein.
b.
The Minimum Rent during each Extension Term shall be as specified in Article
l.rn. of the Lease.
c.
To exercise any option to extend, Tenant must deliver a binding Option Notice to
Landlord not less than ninety (90) days prior to the expiration of the Initial Lease Term of this
Lease, or the current Extension Term, as applicable.
Notwithstanding anything herein to the
contrary, should Tenant fail to timely provide an Option Notice, Landlord will notify Tenant in
writing that it has missed the deadline and Tenant shall have ten (10) days after receipt of such
notice from Landlord to provide Landlord with an Option Notice. if Tenant fails to provide and
Option Notice to Landlord within such ten (10)-day period, Tenant’s option to extend (and any
future options to extend) will be terminated and Tenant will be deemed to have waived its option
to extend.
d.
Tenant’s option to extend the Lease is subject to the conditions that, on the date that
Tenant delivers its binding notice exercising an option to extend, Tenant: (i) is not in default under
the Lease after the expiration of any applicable notice and cure periods; and, (ii) subject to Tenant’s
right to a Permitted Transfer of the Lease which Permitted Transferee shall be allowed to exercise
these options, Tenant shall not have assigned this Lease, or sublet any portion of the Premises under
a sublease which is effective at any time during the final twelve (12) months of the Initial Lease
Term or the first Extension Term, as applicable, to any person or entity.
e.
After exercise of the Extension Terms granted herein, if at all, there shall be no
further rights on the part of Tenant to extend the Term. Tenant’s failure to timely and effectively
exercise any option to extend shall he deemed to revoke all subsequent Extension Terms.
